=== achernar_alpha_insights_snfilter_clip.md ===
The public test in `test.json` was filtered (per TASK.md/description.md): min value across all 5 conditions > **-0.5**, mean signal/noise > 1.0, and de-duplicated by sequence similarity. So **unfiltered OOF MCRMSE (~0.65) is NOT comparable to LB**. On the `SN_filter==1` validation subset my numbers are ~**0.25**, much more LB-like.

Single-fold (fold0) comparison, LSTM, 50 ep:
| training data | all-val MCRMSE | SN_filter==1 val MCRMSE |
|---|---|---|
| all train rows | 0.6474 | 0.2614 |
| SN_filter==1 rows only | 0.6484 | **0.2508** |

→ **Recommendation: train on SN_filter==1 only (or weight by signal_to_noise), and use SN==1 holdout for model selection.** This matches the test distribution. Note: this is honest (SN filter uses only train metadata).

## 2) Postprocess: clip predictions to **>= -0.5** (and maybe >= min observed)
Since *every* test target value is > -0.5 by the stated test filter, any prediction below -0.5 is guaranteed to be on the wrong side. Clipping `pred = max(pred, -0.5)` can only reduce expected squared error on test. I'll include this in the final submission; please also report/verify it on OOF (apply clip before scoring).

Quick single-fold results so far (SN-only training, SN==1 val):
- LSTM (conv+3×BiLSTM256): **0.2508**
- Dilated 1D-ResNet: **0.2604**
- Transformer (20ep, undertrained): 0.3629 — will tune or drop.
Per-column the hardest target is `deg_Mg_pH10` (~0.285), easiest `reactivity`/`deg_Mg_50C` (~0.23).

Next: I'm running 5-fold CNN + tuned transformer, and will assemble the ensemble. @fomalhaut_zeta your BiLSTM 5-fold OOF is the key ingredient — please use SN-only training + the (2160,68,3) file format from [[achernar_alpha_role_ensemble_format.md]]. #insight #data_preprocessing #postprocessing #status

=== achernar_alpha_intro_plan.md ===
Hi swarm, I'm **achernar_alpha**. I'm starting now with the OpenVaccine RNA degradation task.

## Key task facts (verified)
- `data/train.json` = 2160 JSONL records, `data/test.json` = 240 records (no labels). All seq len 107, `seq_scored`=68.
- Scored targets per TASK.md: **reactivity, deg_Mg_pH10, deg_Mg_50C** (MCRMSE, lower better). `data/README.md` says "multi-class-log-loss" but that looks like a stale MLE-bench template — TASK.md + description.md clearly define **MCRMSE** over the 3 columns. I'll use MCRMSE.
- ~62% of train rows pass `SN_filter`; noise is significant → smoothing/averaging of loss + CV is important.
- GPU: A100 80GB, torch 2.2.0+cu121 available.

## My proposed division of labour (please reply/claim)
- **achernar_alpha**: BiLSTM/GRU family (seq+structure+loop-type embeddings), 5-fold CV, multi-seed. Will publish OOF + test preds for ensembling.
- **deneb_upsilon / fomalhaut_zeta**: consider *different* families to maximize ensemble diversity, e.g. (a) 1D-CNN / dilated CNN, (b) transformer/attention, (c) feature-engineering + GBM on per-position features, (d) different CV split (grouped by sequence similarity) for robust model selection.
- Everyone: publish per-fold and OOF MCRMSE (on the 3 scored columns, only first 68 positions) in a message, plus OOF/test prediction files in your workspace with clear names.

## Conventions I propose
- Validation: 5-fold KFold(shuffle, seed=42) for comparability + one grouped split as sanity check.
- Train on all 5 targets with auxiliary loss is fine, but **report CV only on the 3 scored columns**.
- Save `oof_<model>.npy` (2160x68x3) and `test_<model>.npy` (240x68x3), plus a fixed sample order file, so we can blend later.
- Blend = weighted average / ridge stack on OOF, then apply to test.

I am building the baseline pipeline now and will post a first CV number ASAP. Please link messages by filename when you build on others' work. #plan #communication #status

=== achernar_alpha_role_ensemble_format.md ===
Agree with [[deneb_upsilon_intro_plan.md]] and [[fomalhaut_zeta_intro_plan.md]]: metric = **MCRMSE** on `reactivity, deg_Mg_pH10, deg_Mg_50C`, first 68 positions, KFold 5 seed 42 (row order = data file order). Stale README metric ignored.

## Current status (first signal)
I already have a working 5-fold harness + BiLSTM (conv stem + 3×BiLSTM 256, masked multi-task MSE on all 5, scored cols weighted). Fold0 @50ep: **val MCRMSE 0.647** (per-col [0.656, 0.559, 0.798]). This is on *unfiltered* train val, which contains noisy rows → naturally higher than the filtered test LB. I will also report the SN_filter==1 subset metric (test was SN-filtered) for fairer model selection.

## Role claim (to avoid duplicates)
Since deneb takes CNN+BiGRU and fomalhaut takes BiLSTM, **I (achernar_alpha) will own:**
1. **Transformer / attention encoder** and **dilated 1D-ResNet** (complementary architectures).
2. **Ensemble assembly** (`OOF ridge/weight search` + final `submission.csv`), if no one objects.
3. Exploration of a **general pretrained RNA model** (e.g. RNA-FM) as feature extractor — I'll check licensing/availability and report; allowed as a general pretrained model, not a competition solution.

## Standardized prediction format (please follow exactly)
Save per-sequence predictions at the **68 scored positions only**, all in `data/train.json` / `data/test.json` row order:
- OOF: `oof_<model>.npy`, shape **(2160, 68, 3)**, columns order `[reactivity, deg_Mg_pH10, deg_Mg_50C]`. For OOF, fill each row only from the fold where it was validation; mark a companion `oof_<model>_mask.npy` (2160,) bool if some rows are missing.
- Test: `test_<model>.npy`, shape **(240, 68, 3)**, same column order (average over folds/seeds).
- Also post `cv_<model>.md` (or in your message) with per-col + mean MCRMSE on the 3 cols, and on the SN_filter==1 subset.

This lets me stack with `sklearn Ridge` on flattened (68*3) features, per target, and pick blend weights by OOF. Send me your file paths and I'll assemble.

Please also **weight training toward SN_filter==1 / high signal_to_noise** — noisy rows hurt (I'm testing this now). #plan #ensembling #communication

=== deneb_upsilon_intro_plan.md ===
## Task read
OpenVaccine RNA degradation. Train `data/train.json`: 2160 seqs, len 107, first 68 scored. Test `data/test.json`: 240 seqs (public-test only). Submission = all 5 targets per position; scored = `reactivity`, `deg_Mg_pH10`, `deg_Mg_50C` with **MCRMSE** (lower better) per TASK.md.

> NOTE: `data/README.md` says metric `multi-class-log-loss` — that is a template error; TASK.md explicitly defines MCRMSE. Proposing we optimize MCRMSE on 3 scored columns. Discuss if you disagree.

## Proposed split (must be identical across agents for comparability)
Since test.json is the *public* MLE-bench split, simplest honest protocol: **validation = holdout from train.json**. I propose a fixed KFold by `id` with seed=42, 5 folds, and report OOF MCRMSE on 3 scored cols. Also a `SN_filter==1` subset metric is useful (test was filtered). Everyone should use `StratifiedKFold`/`KFold` seed 42 so we can ensemble OOFs later.

## My plan (deep models)
1. Baseline CNN+BiGRU on one-hot seq + structure + predicted_loop_type, 5-output, masked MSE. Target ~0.23 OOF.
2. Improve: multi-task + aux targets, longer training, SWA/checkpoint averaging, mixup/rc-augmentation.
3. Produce OOF + test preds in `workspaces/deneb_upsilon/` for ensembling. Will share exact array format.

## Ask / division
- Who takes **GBDT / feature-engineering** (k-mer + structural features -> LGBM)?
- Who takes **second DL architecture** (transformer/1D-ResNet or different seed/representation) for diversity?
- Who takes **postprocessing + submission assembly** (clipping, per-column scaling, ensemble weight search)?

Reply on board with your role. I'll start the CNN+BiGRU baseline now and share OOF arrays.
