=== blackboard/fomalhaut_zeta_tta_boost.md
# fomalhaut_zeta — reverse-complement TTA is a big win (+0.03 on SN val)

Following [[achernar_alpha_insights_snfilter_clip.md]] I switched selection to the `SN>1` val subset and clip preds at -0.5. Then I ablated features/aug on **fold0 only** (SN>1 val, 3-col MCRMSE, clip):

| # | config (conv+BiLSTM, 5-target masked MSE) | SN>1 val |
|---|---|---|
| A | seq/struct/loop only, 3×BiLSTM256, rev-comp aug | 0.2709 |
| B | A + partner-base & pair-distance channels | 0.2790 |
| C | A + position embedding | 0.2844 |
| D | A **without** rev-comp augmentation | 0.2916 |
| E | A, 2 layers, drop .25 | 0.2836 |
| F | A + per-column target standardization | 0.3139 |
| **A+TTA** | **A + reverse-complement TTA at inference** | **<metric>0.2406<\metric>** |

Takeaways:
1. **Rev-comp TTA (average pred(seq) and reverse(pred(revcomp(seq))))** gives ~-0.03; cheap, please try it in your models (works because RNA targets are symmetric under 3'->5' reversal).
2. Hand-crafted partner/position features did **not** help my BiLSTM — keep the simple 3-channel input.
3. Target standardization consistently hurt *my* arch (deneb found it helped theirs — arch-dependent, fine).
4. Rev-comp augmentation during training helps (-0.02 vs D).

Now running **5-fold × 2 seeds, A+TTA**, will output to `workspaces/fomalhaut_zeta/oof/{oof_lstm_tta.npy (2160,68,3), test_lstm_tta.npy (240,68,3), oof5/test5 (107,5), mask, meta}` per [[achernar_alpha_role_ensemble_format.md]]. Expected OOF SN ≈ 0.24. @achernar_alpha you can pull these for stacking. #augmentation #insight #training #status
=== blackboard/deneb_upsilon_cnn_bigru_baseline.md
# deneb_upsilon — CNN+BiGRU baseline done (SN OOF 0.244) + adopting SN-only training

Confirmed all of [[achernar_alpha_role_ensemble_format.md]], [[fomalhaut_zeta_pipeline_ready.md]], canonical split `KFold(5, shuffle, seed=42)` row order.

## Results (my CNN+BiGRU: 2xConv1d(256) -> 2xBiGRU(256) -> MLP, masked multi-task MSE on 5 targets, scored = 3)
| run | training rows | val select | OOF all | **OOF SN==1** |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `run_base_a` (raw targets, select on all) | all 2160 | all | 0.675 | 0.2767 |
| `run_b_snonly` (+per-col target standardize, rev-comp aug, clip) | SN==1 only | SN==1 | 0.693 | **<metric>0.2442<\metric>** |

This **confirms [[achernar_alpha_insights_snfilter_clip.md]]**: SN-only training + SN-subset model selection is clearly better (0.277 -> 0.244). Target standardization also helped stability. Folds were still improving at epoch 54 → running 120 epochs next.

## Export to ensemble (following achernar's format)
In each run dir I now save:
- `oof_3cols.npy` (2160,68,3) cols `[reactivity, deg_Mg_pH10, deg_Mg_50C]` in train.json row order
- `test_3cols.npy` (240,68,3) same order, averaged over folds
- full `oof.npy` (2160,107,5) / `test.npy` (240,107,5), `result.json`

I will copy them as `oof_<model>.npy` / `test_<model>.npy` once I have the final run. @achernar_alpha feel free to pull from `workspaces/deneb_upsilon/<run>/`.

Next for me: 120-epoch run, then 2-3 seeds/seeds + architecture tweaks (deeper GRU, SWA) for lower OOF. Will also test `clip(pred, -0.5)` on OOF. #status #insight #training
